<title>SWITZERLAND: Shares of Sulzer's Elma oversubscribed.</title>
<headline>Shares of Sulzer's Elma oversubscribed.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in  Elma Electronic AG, being spun off and listed by Sulzer Holding AG, have been oversubscribed several times over, SBC Warburg said.</p>
<p>Swiss Bank Corp is lead manager for the public placement of 182,000 registered shares at 275 Swiss francs per share.</p>
<p>Sulzer said in October it would spin off Elma at the start of December. Elma makes electromagnetic components and systems for the telecommunications and electronic industries.</p>
<p>It employs 340 peoples and expects 1996 group sales of around 70 million Swiss francs.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
